-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 18, DIVISION 5: APPEALS FROM THE GENERAL DIVISION TO THE APPELLATE DIVISION OR THE COURT OF APPEAL, ETC., rules 26 to 41 (roc3, layer 1)
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN` (or `MAYBE DATE`, `MAYBE NUMBER`).
--   JUST TRUE / a value   the text says yes (or names the value) on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE            the text says no in its own words: a flat negative, "only", a period it fixes
--                         in its own words that has run out, an "if", "where" or "unless" read as the
--                         text's no.
--   NOTHING               the text does not answer: it limits a grant by its own wording (a scope with
--                         no "only", a manner, a complement), is silent, or points outside the sources.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- TIME.  A period is a constant of the core type `Period`; timeliness is decided against the input
-- `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` (PLAN.md 5.1, S-T1).  O 3 r 2(1) is not threaded.
-- THE POLARITY OF "UNLESS": for a prohibition ("no oral arguments are to be made unless ...") an order
-- that lifts it makes the answer NOTHING (the prohibition lapses and the paragraph does not say the
-- thing is then allowed); for a requirement or a deeming ("the appeal is deemed withdrawn unless the
-- appellate Court otherwise orders") an order makes it JUST FALSE (fork 18.1).
-- Rules 16, 21, 25 and 33 repeat one another; each has its own functions, named and cited by its own label.


§ `Order 18, Division 5 -- Appeals from General Division to Appellate Division or Court of Appeal, etc. (rules 26 to 41)`

§§ `Rule 26 -- scope of this Division`

DECLARE `o 18 r 26 kind of appeal or application` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 26(a) an appeal to the Appellate Division against a decision of the General Division in an application in an action`
    `o 18 r 26(b) an appeal to the Court of Appeal against a decision of the General Division in an application in an action`
    `o 18 r 26(c) an appeal to the Court of Appeal against a decision of the Appellate Division in an application in an action`
    `o 18 r 26(d) an appeal to the Court of Appeal against a decision of the Appellate Division on an application by summons in an appeal to the Appellate Division under Order 18 or Order 19`
    `o 18 r 26(e) an application to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal relating to an appeal mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)`
    `o 18 r 26 any other appeal or application`

-- src:1988 | 26. This Division applies to — ( a )
-- src:1989 | an appeal to the Appellate Division against any decision of the General Division in relation to an application in an action (including an appeal transferred between the Appellate Division and the Court of Appeal);
-- src:1990 | ( b )
-- src:1991 | an appeal to the Court of Appeal against any decision of the General Division in relation to an application in an action (including an appeal transferred between the Appellate Division and the Court of Appeal);
-- src:1992 | ( c )
-- src:1993 | an appeal to the Court of Appeal against any decision of the Appellate Division in relation to an application in an action;
-- src:1994 | ( d )
-- src:1995 | an appeal to the Court of Appeal against any decision of the Appellate Division on an application by summons in an appeal to the Appellate Division under this Order or Order 19; and
-- src:1996 | ( e )
-- src:1997 | an application to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal relating to an appeal mentioned in paragraph ( a ), ( b ), ( c ) or ( d ).
@ref O 18 r 26 (src:1988-1997)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 18 r 26 kind of appeal or application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 26 this Division applies to the appeal or application` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `o 18 r 26 any other appeal or application`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This Division applies to" the listed appeals and applications; the Rule does not say that it applies to nothing else
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Rule 27 -- bringing of appeal`

-- src:1999 | 27. —(1) A party who intends to appeal to the appellate Court against the decision of the lower Court hearing any application or any appeal must file and serve on all parties who have an interest in the appeal a notice of appeal in Form 35 — ( a )
-- src:2000 | within 14 days after the date of the lower Court’s decision; or
-- src:2001 | ( b )
-- src:2002 | in a case where a request for further arguments has been made under section 29B(2) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act — within 14 days after the date mentioned in section 29B(4)( b ) of that Act.
@ref O 18 r 27(1) (src:1999-2002)
GIVEN `a request for further arguments has been made under section 29B(2) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the lower Court's decision` IS A DATE
      `the date mentioned in section 29B(4)(b) of that Act` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 18 r 27(1) the date after which the 14 days for the notice of appeal run` MEANS
    IF `a request for further arguments has been made under section 29B(2) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act`
    THEN `the date mentioned in section 29B(4)(b) of that Act`
    ELSE JUST `the date of the lower Court's decision` -- limb (a); when a request was made the encoding takes limb (b): fork 18.2

@ref O 18 r 27(1) (src:1999-2002)
`o 18 r 27(1) the period for the notice of appeal` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`
@ref O 18 r 27(1) (src:1999-2002)
GIVEN `the party intends to appeal to the appellate Court against the decision of the lower Court hearing an application or an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of appeal is in Form 35 and is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice of appeal in Form 35 was filed and served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 27(1) the notice of appeal in Form 35 is filed and served in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the party intends to appeal to the appellate Court against the decision of the lower Court hearing an application or an appeal`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A party who intends to appeal to the appellate Court against the decision of the lower Court hearing any application or any appeal"
        IF `the notice of appeal is in Form 35 and is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` AND (`the date the notice of appeal in Form 35 was filed and served` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
