GIVEN `a party applies for permission under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities are filed at the time of filing the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 29(7)(a) the written submissions and any bundle of authorities are filed at the time of filing the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a party applies for permission under this Rule`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A party applying for permission under this Rule"
        IF `written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities are filed at the time of filing the application` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, at the time of filing the application, file written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities"
@ref O 18 r 29(7)(b) (src:2040-2043)
GIVEN `the bundle consists of documents that are relevant to the application and that were filed in the proceedings below` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 29(7)(b) the party may file a bundle of documents with the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the bundle consists of documents that are relevant to the application and that were filed in the proceedings below` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a bundle of documents that are relevant to the application and that were filed in the proceedings below, such as the whole or a part of the notes of evidence, pleadings and affidavits"
@ref O 18 r 29(7) (src:2040-2043)
GIVEN `a party applies for permission under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities are filed at the time of filing the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 29(7) the documents mentioned in paragraph (7) are filed with the application` MEANS
    `o 18 r 29(7)(a) the written submissions and any bundle of authorities are filed at the time of filing the application` `a party applies for permission under this Rule` `written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities are filed at the time of filing the application` -- the seam answer asked by Order 1, rule 2(4)(c) as `o 18 r 29(7) or o 19 r 26(7) the documents mentioned are filed and served with it`: paragraph (7)(b) is a "may", so only (a) is a document that must accompany the application

-- src:2044 | (8) A party who wishes to oppose an application for permission under this Rule — ( a )
-- src:2045 | must file and serve written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities; and
-- src:2046 | ( b )
-- src:2047 | may, together with the written submissions mentioned in sub‑paragraph ( a ), file and serve a bundle of documents that are relevant to the application and that were filed in the proceedings below, such as the whole or a part of the notes of evidence, pleadings and affidavits,
-- src:2048 | within 14 days after the application, written submissions, any accompanying bundle of authorities and bundle of documents mentioned in paragraph (7) are served on the party.
@ref O 18 r 29(8) (src:2044-2048)
`o 18 r 29(8) the period after service of the application for the opposing party’s submissions` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`
@ref O 18 r 29(8) (src:2044-2048)
GIVEN `a party wishes to oppose an application for permission under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities are filed and served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the written submissions and any bundles were filed and served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 29(8) the opposing party's written submissions are filed and served in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a party wishes to oppose an application for permission under this Rule`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A party who wishes to oppose an application for permission under this Rule"
        IF `the written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities are filed and served` AND (`the date the written submissions and any bundles were filed and served` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the application, written submissions, any accompanying bundle of authorities and bundle of documents mentioned in paragraph (7) are served on the party" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
