§§ `Rule 30 -- security for costs`

-- src:2063 | 30. —(1) The appellant must provide security for the respondent’s costs of the appeal and file a certificate for security for costs in Form 36 at the time the appellant files the notice of appeal. (2) Where there is more than one appellant in the same appeal, all the appellants need to provide only one set of security for the appeal.
@ref O 18 r 30(1) (src:2063)
GIVEN `the appellant has provided security for the respondent's costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate for security for costs in Form 36 is filed at the time of filing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 30(1) the appellant has provided security and filed the certificate in Form 36 at the time of filing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appellant has provided security for the respondent's costs` AND `the certificate for security for costs in Form 36 is filed at the time of filing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "file a certificate for security for costs in Form 36 at the time"
-- src:2063 | 30. —(1) The appellant must provide security for the respondent’s costs of the appeal and file a certificate for security for costs in Form 36 at the time the appellant files the notice of appeal. (2) Where there is more than one appellant in the same appeal, all the appellants need to provide only one set of security for the appeal.
@ref O 18 r 30(2) (src:2063)
