        IF `there is more than one appellant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need to provide only one set of security" (a "where" that is not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
-- src:2064 | (3) Where there is more than one respondent, the appellant must provide security for the costs of the appeal for each respondent (or for the costs of the appeal of each set of the respondents where the respondents are represented by the same firm of solicitors).
@ref O 18 r 30(3) (src:2064)
GIVEN `there is more than one respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
