        IF `there is more than one respondent` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is more than one" (a "where" that is not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
@ref O 18 r 30(3) (src:2064)
GIVEN `there is more than one respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondents are represented by the same firm of solicitors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 30(3) the security is provided for each set of respondents represented by the same firm of solicitors` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `there is more than one respondent`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is more than one" (a "where" that is not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF `the respondents are represented by the same firm of solicitors` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "represented by the same firm of solicitors" (a "where" that is not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): the respondents are not represented by one firm, so security is provided for each respondent)
