§§ `Rule 31 -- related appeals`

-- src:2075 | 31. —(1) Where there are related appeals in the appellate Court, the appellate Court may give directions for the filing and service of such joint documents as may be appropriate in the circumstances. (2) The directions in paragraph (1) may be given by the appellate Court on its own motion or on the application or request of any party to any of the related appeals.
@ref O 18 r 31(1) (src:2075)
GIVEN `there are related appeals in the appellate Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 31(1) the appellate Court may give directions for the filing and service of such joint documents as may be appropriate in the circumstances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `there are related appeals in the appellate Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there are related appeals in the appellate Court" (a "where" that is not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
@ref O 18 r 31(2) (src:2075)
`o 18 r 31(2) the directions in paragraph (1) may be given on the appellate Court’s own motion or on the application or request of any party to any of the related appeals` MEANS JUST TRUE
