GIVEN trigger IS A `o 18 r 33(5) what starts the period for the written submissions`
GIVETH A Period
`o 18 r 33(5) the period for the written submissions` MEANS
    CONSIDER trigger
    WHEN `o 18 r 33(5)(a) the notification of the certificate that a written judgment or grounds of decision were already issued` THEN `o 18 r 33(5)(a) the period after the notification`
    WHEN `o 18 r 33(5)(b) the notification that a copy of the written grounds of decision is ready for collection` THEN `o 18 r 33(5)(a) the period after the notification`
    WHEN `o 18 r 33(5)(c) the notification of the certificate that the certified transcript sets out the grounds of decision sufficiently` THEN `o 18 r 33(5)(a) the period after the notification`
    WHEN `o 18 r 33(5)(d) the presumption that no further written grounds of decision will be issued` THEN `o 18 r 33(5)(d) the period after the filing and service of the notice of appeal`
    WHEN `o 18 r 33(5)(e) the notification that the appeal is to proceed after an application to proceed` THEN `o 18 r 33(5)(a) the period after the notification`

