§§ `Rule 34 -- payment out of security for costs and release of undertaking`

-- src:2135 | 34. —(1) This Rule applies without the need for an order from the Court. (2) Where costs are payable by the appellant to the respondent under any order made by the appellate Court, the security for costs provided under Rule 30 must be paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered and the balance (if any) of the security must be paid to the appellant.
@ref O 18 r 34(1) (src:2135)
`o 18 r 34(1) this Rule applies without the need for an order from the Court` MEANS JUST TRUE
@ref O 18 r 34(1) (src:2135)
`o 18 r 34(1) an order from the Court is needed for this Rule to apply` MEANS JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the need for an order from the Court"
@ref O 18 r 34(2) (src:2135)
GIVEN `costs are payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the appellate Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 34(2) the security for costs must be paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `costs are payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the appellate Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where costs are payable by the appellant to the respondent under any order made by the" (a "where" that is not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
GIVEN `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the security for costs provided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 18 r 34(2) the amount of the security paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered` MEANS
    IF `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent` AT MOST `the amount of the security for costs provided`
    THEN `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent`
    ELSE `the amount of the security for costs provided` -- the security is paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered; the whole of it when the costs exceed it
GIVEN `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the security for costs provided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 18 r 34(2) the balance of the security paid to the appellant` MEANS
    IF `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent` AT MOST `the amount of the security for costs provided`
    THEN `the amount of the security for costs provided` MINUS `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent`
    ELSE 0 -- "the balance (if any)"

