§§ `Rule 35 -- applications to appellate Court`

-- src:2139 | 35. —(1) Every application to the appellate Court must be made either by originating application or, in an appeal which is pending before the appellate Court, by summons. (2) Whenever under these Rules an application may be made either to the lower Court or to the appellate Court, it must not be made in the first instance to the appellate Court, except where there are special circumstances which make it impossible or impracticable to apply to the lower Court.
