§§ `Rule 39 -- powers in sections 40(1) and 58(1) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act exercisable by Registrar`

DECLARE `o 18 r 39(1) kind of direction or order` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 39(1)(a) a direction or order for the extension of time to file or serve written submissions pursuant to Rule 33`
    `o 18 r 39(1)(b)(i) a direction or order for the extension of time to file or serve written submissions or affidavits in any application`
    `o 18 r 39(1)(b)(ii) a direction or order for the extension of time to file or serve a bundle of authorities in any appeal or application`
    `o 18 r 39(1)(b)(iii) a direction or order for the extension of time to file or serve a bundle of documents in any application for permission to appeal`
    `o 18 r 39(1)(c) a direction under Rule 31(1)`
    `o 18 r 39(1)(d) a direction or order for the amendment of any document filed for any appeal or application`
    `o 18 r 39(1)(e) a direction or order relating to expunging any document filed for any appeal or application, and consequential directions`
    `o 18 r 39(1)(f) a direction or order relating to the rescheduling of any hearing`
    `o 18 r 39(1) any other direction or order`

-- src:2179 | 39. —(1) The Registrar may exercise the powers of the Appellate Division and the Court of Appeal in sections 40(1)( a ) and 58(1)( a ) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act in the following circumstances: ( a )
-- src:2180 | where the direction or order is for the extension of time to file or serve written submissions pursuant to Rule 33, and all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order;
-- src:2181 | ( b )
-- src:2182 | where the direction or order is for the extension of time to file or serve any of the following documents: (i)
-- src:2183 | written submissions or affidavits in any application;
-- src:2184 | (ii)
-- src:2185 | a bundle of authorities in any appeal or application;
-- src:2186 | (iii)
-- src:2187 | a bundle of documents in any application for permission to appeal;
-- src:2188 | ( c )
-- src:2189 | where the direction is a direction under Rule 31(1);
-- src:2190 | ( d )
-- src:2191 | where the direction or order is for the amendment of any document filed for any appeal or application, and all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order;
-- src:2192 | ( e )
-- src:2193 | where the direction or order relates to expunging any document filed for any appeal or application, and all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order, and for consequential directions in relation to the direction or order;
-- src:2194 | ( f )
-- src:2195 | where the direction or order relates to the rescheduling of any hearing.
@ref O 18 r 39(1) (src:2179-2195)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 18 r 39(1) kind of direction or order`
      `all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 39(1) the Registrar may exercise the powers of the Appellate Division and the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `o 18 r 39(1)(a) a direction or order for the extension of time to file or serve written submissions pursuant to Rule 33` THEN IF `all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order"
    WHEN `o 18 r 39(1)(b)(i) a direction or order for the extension of time to file or serve written submissions or affidavits in any application` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 18 r 39(1)(b)(ii) a direction or order for the extension of time to file or serve a bundle of authorities in any appeal or application` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 18 r 39(1)(b)(iii) a direction or order for the extension of time to file or serve a bundle of documents in any application for permission to appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 18 r 39(1)(c) a direction under Rule 31(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 18 r 39(1)(d) a direction or order for the amendment of any document filed for any appeal or application` THEN IF `all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order"
    WHEN `o 18 r 39(1)(e) a direction or order relating to expunging any document filed for any appeal or application, and consequential directions` THEN IF `all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order"
    WHEN `o 18 r 39(1)(f) a direction or order relating to the rescheduling of any hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 18 r 39(1) any other direction or order` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the following circumstances" (the circumstances listed; the paragraph does not say that no other is allowed)

-- src:2196 | (2) An application to vary or discharge any direction or order of the Registrar under paragraph (1) may be made to a single Judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal (as the case may be), and any such application must be filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal within 14 days after the date on which that direction or order is made, and the decision of that Judge is final.
