DECLARE `o 18 r 40(5) matter the Court of Appeal may have regard to` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 40(5)(a) whether the proceedings relate to a matter of national or public importance`
    `o 18 r 40(5)(b) whether the appeal will raise a point of law of public importance`
    `o 18 r 40(5)(c) the complexity and novelty of the issues in the appeal`
    `o 18 r 40(5)(d) whether there is a decision of the Court of Appeal in relation to a point of law raised in the appeal which may be material to the outcome of the appeal`
    `o 18 r 40(5)(e) whether there are conflicting judicial decisions`
    `o 18 r 40(5)(f) the significance of the results of the proceedings`
    `o 18 r 40(5)(g) any other relevant matter`

